```javascript
function onMouseOver(event) {
  var element = document.getElementById('element');
  if (element && element.style.backgroundColor === 'red') {
    element.style.backgroundColor = 'green';
  } else {
    element.style.backgroundColor = 'black';
  }
}
```

This code creates an event handler for the mouse over event on the element with ID "element". If the background color of the element is red, it will change to green; otherwise, it will stay black. You can modify this code to suit your needs by changing the CSS styles and the element IDs.

